# Document and sections: Begin on: odd starts a section on a right-hand page, adding a blank page when needed.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Document and sections · Begin on an odd page
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Page overlay:
		Offset: auto 0 -24 0
		Text: Page {page} of {pages}
			Typography:
				Align: right
	Section:
		Text: Document and sections
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Begin on an odd page
		Paragraph: With `Begin on: odd`, a section starts on an odd page, the right-hand one in double-sided printing. Here the first chapter ends on page 1, so the engine adds page 2 blank: it counts for the numbers but carries no content and no footer.
			Style: intro
		Heading 2:
			Text: Chapter 1
		Paragraph: The first chapter takes up a single page.
	Section:
		Begin on: odd
		Heading 2:
			Text: Chapter 2
		Text: Begin on: odd  (this is page 3)
			Style: card
		Paragraph: Page 2, before this one, is the blank page that the engine added.
	Section:
		Begin on: any
		Heading 2:
			Text: Chapter 3
		Text: Begin on: any  (the default: the next page, page 4)
			Style: card
